          "answer": "By the Intersecting Chords Theorem (Power of a Point Theorem), when two chords \\(AB\\) and \\(CD\\) intersect at an interior point \\(P\\), the products of their segments are equal:\n\\[\nPA \\cdot PB = PC \\cdot PD\n\\]\nSubstitute the given values into the equation:\n\\[\n(4)(6) = (3)(PD)\n\\]\n\\[\n24 = 3 \\cdot PD\n\\]\n\\[\nPD = \\frac{24}{3} = 8\n\\]\n\nCommon error analysis:\n- Adding the segment lengths instead of multiplying (\\(PA + PB = PC + PD \\implies 4 + 6 = 3 + PD \\implies PD = 7\\)) yields 7, which fails because the segments satisfy a multiplicative relationship derived from similar triangles (\\(\\triangle PAD \\sim \\triangle PCB\\)).",
